# Conventional Commits

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/). Match this org’s history (`feat:`, `docs(validation):`, `chore:`).

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]
```

| Type | Use when |
|---|---|
| `feat` | User-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Tooling, config, deps; no product change |
| `refactor` | Structure change, same behaviour |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `ci` | CI/CD |
| `revert` | Revert a previous commit |

Scope is optional kebab-case (`docs(validation): …`).

- Imperative, lowercase: `add`, not `Added` or `adds`
- No trailing period
- ~72 characters; wrap the body at 72
- Body (after a blank line) explains **why**, not what

```
feat: publish enforced MTA-STS policy
docs(validation): hedge outreach claims
chore: skip Jekyll on GitHub Pages
```

Do not mix unrelated changes. Do not invent types. Do not rewrite published history unless asked.
